# Committed on purpose. Every value here is PUBLIC_-prefixed, which means Astro
# bakes it into the shipped HTML anyway - the CDN host and the GTM container ID
# are both readable by anyone who views source. Neither is a credential.
#
# Why version them instead of setting them in the Cloudflare Pages dashboard:
# the dashboard is invisible from the repo. A build that silently loses
# PUBLIC_CDN_URL falls back to same-origin images, and one that loses
# PUBLIC_GTM_ID drops analytics with no error anywhere. Keeping them here makes
# every build - local, CI, or a fresh clone - produce the same site.
#
# Real secrets never belong in this file. They go in .env (gitignored) for
# local use and in the Pages dashboard or `wrangler pages secret put` for
# production.

PUBLIC_CDN_URL=https://pub-29b2020ad2a44fcfb6073ca4a9925842.r2.dev

# GTM_ID is deliberately NOT here. It is owned by the Cloudflare Pages
# dashboard under "Variables and secrets" so it can be edited without a commit.
# See the GTM_ID comment in src/consts.ts.
